meta\">\n   314→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Research Data</span>\n   315→                            </div>\n   316→                        </div>\n   317→                    </div>\n   318→                </section>\n   319→\n   320→                <!-- Whitelist Updates Section (35%) -->\n   321→                <section class=\"column whitelist-updates\" id=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   322→                    <div class=\"section-header\">Product Updates</div>\n   323→                    <div class=\"section-content\">\n   324→                        <!-- GitHub Copilot Model Deprecations -->\n   325→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   326→                            <span class=\"update-badge update-announcement\">ANNOUNCEMENT</span>\n   327→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   328→                                <a href=\"https://github.com/github/roadmap/issues/1308\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot - Model deprecations announced</a>\n   329→                            </div>\n   330→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   331→                                Several Copilot models will retire on September 1, 2026. Enterprise admins must enable replacement models before the deadline.\n   332→                            </div>\n   333→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   334→                                <span class=\"item-source\">GitHub Roadmap</span>\n   335→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-31</span>\n   336→                            </div>\n   337→                            <div class=\"feedback\">\n   338→                                <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Goodbye, Copilot. Github Copilot won't be around in a year or two because of their absolute incompetence\"</div>\n   339→                                <div class=\"feedback-source\">Reddit (negative sentiment)</div>\n   340→                            </div>\n   341→                            <div class=\"feedback\">\n   342→                                <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Adopters merge roughly 24% more pull requests over four months\"</div>\n   343→                                <div class=\"feedback-source\">HN (positive sentiment)</div>\n   344→                            </div>\n   345→                        </div>\n   346→\n   347→                        <!-- Cursor Updates -->\n   348→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   349→                            <span class=\"update-badge update-feature\">FEATURE</span>\n   350→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   351→                                <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor - Origin Code Hosting, Cloud Agents, and iPad app</a>\n   352→                            </div>\n   353→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   354→                                Launches Origin code hosting (early beta), cloud agents with subscriptions and custom modes, 3x faster agent starts with builds, Google Workspace plugins, and redesigned iPad experience.\n   355→                            </div>\n   356→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   357→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Cursor Changelog</span>\n   358→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-19</span>\n   359→                            </div>\n   360→                            <div class=\"feedback\">\n   361→                                <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"A few hours earlier and you'd have a git platform when GitHub didn't\"</div>\n   362→                                <div class=\"feedback-source\">Reddit</div>\n   363→                            </div>\n   364→                            <div class=\"feedback\">\n   365→                                <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Designed around increasingly autonomous coding agents\"</div>\n   366→                                <div class=\"feedback-source\">Reddit (positive sentiment)</div>\n   367→                            </div>\n   368→                        </div>\n   369→\n   370→                        <!-- GitHub Copilot Weekly Release -->\n   371→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   372→                            <span class=\"update-badge update-release\">RELEASE</span>\n   373→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   374→                                <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-13-github-copilot-weekly-releases-august-10/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot - Weekly releases (August 10, 2026)</a>\n   375→                            </div>\n   376→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   377→                                Kimi K3 and MAI-Code-1.1-Flash models rolling out; Agent Plugins 1.0 now generally available; improved plugin management in app; CLI enhancements with /tasks and queued prompts; JetBrains gets Copilot memory and Ollama support.\n   378→                            </div>\n   379→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   380→                                <span class=\"item-source\">GitHub Blog</span>\n   381→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-13</span>\n   382→                            </div>\n   383→                            <div class=\"feedback\">\n   384→                                <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Did GitHub's Copilot get a huge upgrade in the last few weeks? It now consistently finds real issues and is genuinely helpful\"</div>\n   385→                                <div class=\"feedback-source\">X/Twitter (DHH) - positive sentiment</div>\n   386→                            </div>\n   387→                        </div>\n   388→\n   389→                        <!-- Devin Coach Feature -->\n   390→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   391→                            <span class=\"update-badge update-feature\">FEATURE</span>\n   392→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   393→                                <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\" target=\"_blank\">Devin - Devin Coach feature</a>\n   394→                            </div>\n   395→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   396→                                Devin released a new feature called 'Devin Coach' on August 14, 2026. Specific details about the feature are limited in the available sources.\n   397→                            </div>\n   398→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   399→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Devin Docs</span>\n   400→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-14</span>\n   401→                            </div>\n   402→                        </div>\n   403→\n   404→                        <!-- Claude Code Updates -->\n   405→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   406→                            <span class=\"update-badge update-feature\">FEATURE</span>\n   407→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   408→                                <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code - Cross-session messaging and self-hosted environments</a>\n   409→                            </div>\n   410→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   411→                                v2.1.220–v2.1.224: Cross-session messaging allows sessions to communicate on macOS/Linux; self-hosted environments now in public beta for Team/Enterprise plans; auto mode becomes default starting August 14; VS Code extension gets Focus view.\n   412→                            </div>\n   413→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   414→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Claude Code Docs</span>\n   415→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-07</span>\n   416→                            </div>\n   417→                            <div class=\"feedback\">\n   418→                                <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"You simply tell Claude what the other session needs to know, and it writes and sends the message automatically\"</div>\n   419→                                <div class=\"feedback-source\">Medium (positive sentiment)</div>\n   420→                            </div>\n   421→                            <div class=\"feedback\">\n   422→                                <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Testing showed auto mode blocked 80%+ of dangerous queries while humans only caught 14%\"</div>\n   423→                                <div class=\"feedback-source\">Reddit (positive sentiment)</div>\n   424→                            </div>\n   425→                            <div class=\"feedback\">\n   426→                                <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Anthropic's confidence in Claude Code's auto mode is notable\"</div>\n   427→                                <div class=\"feedback-source\">Simon Willison (positive sentiment)</div>\n   428→                            </div>\n   429→                        </div>\n   430→                    </div>\n   431→                </section>\n   432→\n   433→                <!-- Technical Insights Section (25%) -->\n   434→                <section class=\"column technical-insights\" id=\"technical-insights\">\n   435→                    <div class=\"section-header\">Technical Insights</div>\n   436→                    <div class=\"section-content\">\n   437→                        <!-- Huzzah AI Coding Approach -->\n   438→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   439→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   440→                                <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Show HN: Huzzah – Novel AI Coding Approach</a>\n   441→                            </div>\n   442→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   443→                                New method for programming with AI assistance. Community discussion with 196 points and 110 comments.\n   444→                            </div>\n   445→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   446→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Hacker News</span>\n   447→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-19</span>\n   448→                            </div>\n   449→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   450→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">AI coding</span>\n   451→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">Show HN</span>\n   452→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">programming tools</span>\n   453→                            </div>\n   454→                        </div>\n   455→\n   456→                        <!-- Stop Anthropomorphizing Tokens -->\n   457→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   458→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   459→                                <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Stop Anthropomorphizing Intermediate Tokens</a>\n   460→                            </div>\n   461→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   462→                                Paper argues against interpreting middle tokens as reasoning. 189 points, 105 comments on Hacker News.\n   463→                            </div>\n   464→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   465→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Hacker News</span>\n   466→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-18</span>\n   467→                            </div>\n   468→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   469→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">LLM</span>\n   470→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">tokens</span>\n   471→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">reasoning</span>\n   472→                            </div>\n   473→                        </div>\n   474→\n   475→                        <!-- Vomit Claude Token Output -->\n   476→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   477→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   478→                                <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Vomit: Cleaning Claude 5 Token Output</a>\n   479→                            </div>\n   480→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   481→                                Uses separate LLM to refine another model's output. 169 points, 184 comments discussing the technique.\n   482→                            </div>\n   483→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   484→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Hacker News</span>\n   485→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-17</span>\n   486→                            </div>\n   487→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   488→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">Claude</span>\n   489→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">LLM</span>\n   490→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">output refinement</span>\n   491→                            </div>\n   492→                        </div>\n   493→\n   494→                        <!-- Qwen 3.8 Performance -->\n   495→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   496→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   497→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Qwen 3.8 27B matches GPT-5.6 Luna performance</a>\n   498→                            </div>\n   499→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   500→                                Qwen 3.8 27B stands out as an impressive Apache 2-licensed 27B model that scores 52 on Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index—matching GPT-5.6 Luna.\n   501→                            </div>\n   502→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   503→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   504→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-18</span>\n   505→                            </div>\n   506→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   507→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">LLM</span>\n   508→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">open-source</span>\n   509→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">model evaluation</span>\n   510→                            </div>\n   511→                        </div>\n   512→\n   513→                        <!-- ComponentBench -->\n   514→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   515→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   516→                                <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\" target=\"_blank\">ComponentBench: Diagnosing Component-Level Failures in Computer-Use Agents</a>\n   517→                            </div>\n   518→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   519→                                Accepted at COLM 2026. Benchmark for testing agent components at the component level.\n   520→                            </div>\n   521→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   522→                                <span class=\"item-source\">ArXiv</span>\n   523→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-20</span>\n   524→                            </div>\n   525→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   526→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">agents</span>\n   527→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">benchmarks</span>\n   528→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">COLM 2026</span>\n   529→                            </div>\n   530→                        </div>\n   531→\n   532→                        <!-- Every Model Cheats -->\n   533→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   534→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   535→                                <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Every Model Cheats</a>\n   536→                            </div>\n   537→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   538→                                Research on prompt-level mitigation of model cheating behaviors. 75 points, 56 comments discussing the findings.\n   539→                            </div>\n   540→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   541→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Hacker News</span>\n   542→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-16</span>\n   543→                            </div>\n   544→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   545→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">LLM</span>\n   546→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">safety</span>\n   547→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">adversarial</span>\n   548→                            </div>\n   549→                        </div>\n   550→\n   551→                        <!-- ChatGPT Search Site Operator -->\n   552→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   553→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   554→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">ChatGPT Search site: operator usage surge</a>\n   555→                            </div>\n   556→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   557→                                ChatGPT Search now uses the site: operator at scale. Usage jumped from 0.3-0.5% to 16-17% around August 8, correlating with GPT-5.6 Sol rollout.\n   558→                            </div>\n   559→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   560→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   561→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-18</span>\n   562→                            </div>\n   563→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   564→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">AI search</span>\n   565→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">ChatGPT</span>\n   566→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">usage statistics</span>\n   567→                            </div>\n   568→                        </div>\n   569→\n   570→                        <!-- Jagged Frontier -->\n   571→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   572→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   573→                                <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\" target=\"_blank\">A Jagged Frontier: Evaluating Robustness of Code Agents</a>\n   574→                            </div>\n   575→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   576→                                Evaluates code agents against transformations that preserve semantics. Authors from Colorado State University, Microsoft, UIIL, and Carnegie Mellon.\n   577→                            </div>\n   578→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   579→                                <span class=\"item-source\">ArXiv</span>\n   580→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-20</span>\n   581→                            </div>\n   582→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   583→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">code agents</span>\n   584→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">robustness</span>\n   585→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">evaluation</span>\n   586→                            </div>\n   587→                        </div>\n   588→\n   589→                        <!-- Bun 1.4 WebView -->\n   590→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   591→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   592→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Bun 1.4 adds Bun.WebView for browser automation</a>\n   593→                            </div>\n   594→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   595→                                Bun 1.4 adds Bun.WebView for browser automation, with Simon prototyping a web API that loads pages and executes JavaScript.\n   596→                            </div>\n   597→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   598→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   599→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-14</span>\n   600→                            </div>\n   601→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   602→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">Bun</span>\n   603→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">browser automation</span>\n   604→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">JavaScript</span>\n   605→                            </div>\n   606→                        </div>\n   607→\n   608→                        <!-- Encrypted Reasoning Traces -->\n   609→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   610→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   611→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Encrypted reasoning traces security vulnerability</a>\n   612→                            </div>\n   613→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   614→                                Research revealed encrypted reasoning traces from proprietary APIs could be extracted by replaying them into weaker model family members.\n   615→                            </div>\n   616→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   617→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   618→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-16</span>\n   619→                            </div>\n   620→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   621→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">security</span>\n   622→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">LLM</span>\n   623→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">API vulnerabilities</span>\n   624→                            </div>\n   625→                        </div>\n   626→                    </div>\n   627→                </section>\n   628→            </div>\n   629→        </main>\n   630→\n   631→        <footer>\n   632→            <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n   633→            <a href=\"#\">Archive</a>\n   634→            <a href=\"#\">RSS Feed</a>\n   635→            <a href=\"#\">Contact</a>\n   636→            <div style=\"margin-top: 10px; color: #828282; font-size: 11px;\">\n   637→                Generated with Claude Code | Agentic Coding Research Report\n   638→            </div>\n   639→        </footer>\n   640→    </div>\n   641→</body>\n   642→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
