al Insights</a></li>\n   322→            </ul>\n   323→        </nav>\n   324→\n   325→        <main>\n   326→            <div class=\"three-column-layout\">\n   327→                <!-- New Products Section (40%) -->\n   328→                <section class=\"column new-products\" id=\"new-products\">\n   329→                    <div class=\"section-header\">New Products & Tools</div>\n   330→                    <div class=\"section-content\">\n   331→                        <div class=\"empty-state\">\n   332→                            No new products reported in this period\n   333→                        </div>\n   334→                    </div>\n   335→                </section>\n   336→\n   337→                <!-- Whitelist Updates Section (35%) -->\n   338→                <section class=\"column whitelist-updates\" id=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   339→                    <div class=\"section-header\">Product Updates</div>\n   340→                    <div class=\"section-content\">\n   341→                        <!-- Devin Coach Feature -->\n   342→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   343→                            <span class=\"update-badge update-feature\">FEATURE</span>\n   344→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   345→                                <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\" target=\"_blank\">Devin - Devin Coach feature</a>\n   346→                            </div>\n   347→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   348→                                Devin released a new feature called 'Devin Coach' on August 14, 2026. Specific details about the feature are limited in the available sources.\n   349→                            </div>\n   350→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   351→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Devin Docs</span>\n   352→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-14</span>\n   353→                            </div>\n   354→                        </div>\n   355→\n   356→                        <!-- GitHub Copilot Weekly Release -->\n   357→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   358→                            <span class=\"update-badge update-release\">RELEASE</span>\n   359→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   360→                                <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-13-github-copilot-weekly-releases-august-10/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot - Weekly releases (August 10, 2026)</a>\n   361→                            </div>\n   362→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   363→                                Kimi K3 and MAI-Code-1.1-Flash models rolling out; Agent Plugins 1.0 now generally available; improved plugin management in app; CLI enhancements with /tasks and queued prompts; JetBrains gets Copilot memory and Ollama support.\n   364→                            </div>\n   365→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   366→                                <span class=\"item-source\">GitHub Blog</span>\n   367→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-13</span>\n   368→                            </div>\n   369→                            <div class=\"feedback\">\n   370→                                <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Agent Plugins 1.0 is a real plugin system, not just a roadmap promise\"</div>\n   371→                                <div class=\"feedback-source sentiment-positive\">DEV Community (positive)</div>\n   372→                            </div>\n   373→                            <div class=\"feedback\">\n   374→                                <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Existing GitHub Copilot plugins that don't target Agent Plugins 1.0 continue to work, so you can migrate when it makes sense\"</div>\n   375→                                <div class=\"feedback-source sentiment-positive\">X/Twitter (positive)</div>\n   376→                            </div>\n   377→                            <div class=\"feedback\">\n   378→                                <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Did GitHub's Copilot get a huge upgrade in the last few weeks? It now consistently finds real issues and is genuinely helpful\"</div>\n   379→                                <div class=\"feedback-source sentiment-positive\">X/Twitter (DHH) (positive)</div>\n   380→                            </div>\n   381→                        </div>\n   382→\n   383→                        <!-- Claude Code Updates -->\n   384→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   385→                            <span class=\"update-badge update-feature\">FEATURE</span>\n   386→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   387→                                <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code - Cross-session messaging and self-hosted environments</a>\n   388→                            </div>\n   389→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   390→                                v2.1.220–v2.1.224 (August 3–7, 2026): Cross-session messaging allows sessions to communicate on macOS/Linux; self-hosted environments now in public beta for Team/Enterprise plans; auto mode becomes default starting August 14; VS Code extension gets Focus view.\n   391→                            </div>\n   392→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   393→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Claude Code Docs</span>\n   394→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-07</span>\n   395→                            </div>\n   396→                            <div class=\"feedback\">\n   397→                                <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"I built a general version of this, with global addresses and messaging between any terminal-based agent + MCP for browser agents\"</div>\n   398→                                <div class=\"feedback-source sentiment-positive\">HN (positive)</div>\n   399→                            </div>\n   400→                            <div class=\"feedback\">\n   401→                                <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"You simply tell Claude what the other session needs to know, and it writes and sends the message automatically\"</div>\n   402→                                <div class=\"feedback-source sentiment-positive\">Medium (positive)</div>\n   403→                            </div>\n   404→                            <div class=\"feedback\">\n   405→                                <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Claude Code efficiency feels noticeably worse - significantly less efficient/reliable over recent weeks\"</div>\n   406→                                <div class=\"feedback-source sentiment-negative\">Reddit (negative)</div>\n   407→                            </div>\n   408→                            <div class=\"feedback\">\n   409→                                <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Testing showed auto mode blocked 80%+ of dangerous queries while humans only caught 14%\"</div>\n   410→                                <div class=\"feedback-source sentiment-positive\">Reddit (positive)</div>\n   411→                            </div>\n   412→                            <div class=\"feedback\">\n   413→                                <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"The promotion was the only thing making Claude usable\"</div>\n   414→                                <div class=\"feedback-source sentiment-negative\">Reddit (negative)</div>\n   415→                            </div>\n   416→                            <div class=\"feedback\">\n   417→                                <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Anthropic's confidence in Claude Code's auto mode is notable\"</div>\n   418→                                <div class=\"feedback-source sentiment-positive\">Simon Willison (positive)</div>\n   419→                            </div>\n   420→                            <div class=\"feedback\">\n   421→                                <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Service disruption on August 16, 2026 affected Claude Code and other services\"</div>\n   422→                                <div class=\"feedback-source sentiment-negative\">Reddit (negative)</div>\n   423→                            </div>\n   424→                            <div class=\"feedback\">\n   425→                                <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Sessions can message each other, and Claude sends a summary (not full history or files) when communicating\"</div>\n   426→                                <div class=\"feedback-source sentiment-neutral\">X/Twitter (neutral)</div>\n   427→                            </div>\n   428→                        </div>\n   429→                    </div>\n   430→                </section>\n   431→\n   432→                <!-- Technical Insights Section (25%) -->\n   433→                <section class=\"column technical-insights\" id=\"technical-insights\">\n   434→                    <div class=\"section-header\">Technical Insights</div>\n   435→                    <div class=\"section-content\">\n   436→                        <!-- Stop Making TUIs -->\n   437→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   438→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   439→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Stop Making TUIs - Native UIs for AI Coding Era</a>\n   440→                            </div>\n   441→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   442→                                Thomas Ptacek advocates for building real native user interfaces for even the smallest of personal tools, because coding agents have reduced the cost of getting a usable-enough GUI up and running to almost nothing. Simon notes he's still using his vibe-coded bandwidth and GPU monitoring macOS task bar apps built in March.\n   443→                            </div>\n   444→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   445→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison (Blog)</span>\n   446→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-21</span>\n   447→                            </div>\n   448→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   449→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">vibe-coding</span>\n   450→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">coding-agents</span>\n   451→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">native UIs</span>\n   452→                            </div>\n   453→                        </div>\n   454→\n   455→                        <!-- ChatGPT Search Site Operator -->\n   456→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   457→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   458→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">ChatGPT search now uses the site: operator at scale</a>\n   459→                            </div>\n   460→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   461→                                Promptwatch tracking shows ChatGPT Search usage of site: operator jumped from 0.3-0.5% to 16-17% around August 8, correlating with GPT-5.6 Sol rollout. On August 18th, Promptwatch reported ChatGPT appeared to have greatly reduced the likelihood of Reddit being used in those searches.\n   462→                            </div>\n   463→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   464→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison (Blog)</span>\n   465→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-20</span>\n   466→                            </div>\n   467→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   468→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">chatgpt</span>\n   469→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">search</span>\n   470→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">site:operator</span>\n   471→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">openai</span>\n   472→                            </div>\n   473→                        </div>\n   474→\n   475→                        <!-- Bun 1.4 WebView -->\n   476→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   477→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   478→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Bun 1.4 adds Bun.WebView for browser automation</a>\n   479→                            </div>\n   480→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   481→                                Bun 1.4 release adds Bun.WebView for first-class browser automation support using either macOS WebKit or control of a local Chromium process via CDP. Simon prototyped a web API with Claude Code for web that loads pages and executes JavaScript, inspired by shot-scraper.\n   482→                            </div>\n   483→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   484→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison (Blog)</span>\n   485→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-20</span>\n   486→                            </div>\n   487→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   488→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">bun</span>\n   489→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">javascript</span>\n   490→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">browsers</span>\n   491→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">coding-agents</span>\n   492→                            </div>\n   493→                        </div>\n   494→\n   495→                        <!-- smolmachines sandbox -->\n   496→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   497→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   498→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">smolmachines / smolvm as a sandbox for untrusted Python & JavaScript</a>\n   499→                            </div>\n   500→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   501→                                Research task testing smolmachines.com as a fast secure sandbox for running untrusted Python and JavaScript code with limits on RAM, CPU time, no network access, and controlled filesystem access. Claude Fable 5 creatively worked around Claude Code for web environment limits by running tests via GitHub Actions.\n   502→                            </div>\n   503→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   504→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison (Blog)</span>\n   505→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-19</span>\n   506→                            </div>\n   507→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   508→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">research</span>\n   509→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">sandboxing</span>\n   510→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">claude-mythos-fable</span>\n   511→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">github-actions</span>\n   512→                            </div>\n   513→                        </div>\n   514→\n   515→                        <!-- Mojo Open Source -->\n   516→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   517→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   518→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Mojo🔥 is now open source</a>\n   519→                            </div>\n   520→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   521→                                Mojo programming language released compiler and toolchain under Apache 2 license. Originally planned as Python superset, that plan changed around August 2025. Today Mojo is its own language optimized for GPU programming with Python-inspired syntax.\n   522→                            </div>\n   523→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   524→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison (Blog)</span>\n   525→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-18</span>\n   526→                            </div>\n   527→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   528→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">mojo</span>\n   529→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">open-source</span>\n   530→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">python</span>\n   531→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">gpu-programming</span>\n   532→                            </div>\n   533→                        </div>\n   534→\n   535→                        <!-- Qwen 3.8 Performance -->\n   536→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   537→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   538→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Qwen 3.8 27B scores 52 on Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index</a>\n   539→                            </div>\n   540→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   541→                                Qwen 3.8 27B matches GPT-5.6 Luna performance (score 52), just one point behind GLM-5.2 (753B) and DeepSeek V4 Pro 0813 (1.7T). Qwen is a truly astonishing 27B parameter Apache 2 licensed model.\n   542→                            </div>\n   543→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   544→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison (Blog)</span>\n   545→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-17</span>\n   546→                            </div>\n   547→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   548→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">qwen</span>\n   549→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">llm</span>\n   550→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">local-llms</span>\n   551→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">open-source</span>\n   552→                            </div>\n   553→                        </div>\n   554→\n   555→                        <!-- Amazon AI Training Books -->\n   556→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   557→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   558→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">We Tracked a Shipment of Rare Books. It Ended at an Amazon AI Training Facility</a>\n   559→                            </div>\n   560→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   561→                                404 Media investigated with an AirTag where large-volume book orders from anonymous suspected AI training customers actually go. The book ended at Amazon's LAS8 facility in Las Vegas, confirmed by worker discussions to destructively scan large volumes of books for AI training.\n   562→                            </div>\n   563→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   564→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison (Blog)</span>\n   565→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-17</span>\n   566→                            </div>\n   567→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   568→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">amazon</span>\n   569→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">journalism</span>\n   570→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai-ethics</span>\n   571→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">404-media</span>\n   572→                            </div>\n   573→                        </div>\n   574→\n   575→                        <!-- Qwen Overthinking -->\n   576→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   577→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   578→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Qwen 3.8 27B is excellent, but it defaults to wildly overthinking things</a>\n   579→                            </div>\n   580→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   581→                                Friday's big release Qwen 3.8 27B is an Apache 2 licensed 27B parameter vision-capable LLM from Alibaba. While impressive, it tends to 'wildly overthink' things by default. 27B is an excellent size for running on reasonably specced laptops.\n   582→                            </div>\n   583→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   584→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison (Blog)</span>\n   585→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-16</span>\n   586→                            </div>\n   587→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   588→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">qwen</span>\n   589→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">llm</span>\n   590→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">local-llms</span>\n   591→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">llm-reasoning</span>\n   592→                            </div>\n   593→                        </div>\n   594→\n   595→                        <!-- CORS Chat Tool -->\n   596→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   597→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   598→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">CORS Chat tool for testing local models</a>\n   599→                            </div>\n   600→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   601→                                Built with GPT-5.6-Sol xhigh to test Qwen 3.8 27B running in LM Studio on both M5 MacBook Pro and NVIDIA DGX Spark. Provides web UI for OpenAI-Responses-compatible chat endpoints, supports SVG progressive rendering, exports conversations as JSON.\n   602→                            </div>\n   603→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   604→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison (Blog)</span>\n   605→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-15</span>\n   606→                            </div>\n   607→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   608→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">cors</span>\n   609→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">llms</span>\n   610→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">svg</span>\n   611→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">generative-ai</span>\n   612→                            </div>\n   613→                        </div>\n   614→\n   615→                        <!-- Show HN: Huzzah -->\n   616→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   617→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   618→                                <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Show HN: Huzzah – Novel AI Coding Approach</a>\n   619→                            </div>\n   620→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   621→                                New method for programming with AI assistance. Community discussion with 196 points and 110 comments.\n   622→                            </div>\n   623→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   624→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Hacker News</span>\n   625→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-19</span>\n   626→                            </div>\n   627→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   628→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">AI coding</span>\n   629→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">Show HN</span>\n   630→                            </div>\n   631→                        </div>\n   632→\n   633→                        <!-- Stop Anthropomorphizing Tokens -->\n   634→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   635→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   636→                                <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Stop Anthropomorphizing Intermediate Tokens</a>\n   637→                            </div>\n   638→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   639→                                Paper argues against interpreting middle tokens as reasoning. 189 points, 105 comments on Hacker News.\n   640→                            </div>\n   641→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   642→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Hacker News</span>\n   643→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-18</span>\n   644→                            </div>\n   645→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   646→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">LLM</span>\n   647→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">interpretation</span>\n   648→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">tokens</span>\n   649→                            </div>\n   650→                        </div>\n   651→\n   652→                        <!-- Vomit Claude Token -->\n   653→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   654→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   655→                                <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Vomit: Cleaning Claude 5 Token Output</a>\n   656→                            </div>\n   657→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   658→                                Uses separate LLM to refine another model's output. 169 points, 184 comments discussing the technique.\n   659→                            </div>\n   660→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   661→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Hacker News</span>\n   662→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-17</span>\n   663→                            </div>\n   664→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   665→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">Claude</span>\n   666→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">LLM</span>\n   667→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">output refinement</span>\n   668→                            </div>\n   669→                        </div>\n   670→\n   671→                        <!-- Every Model Cheats -->\n   672→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   673→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   674→                                <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Every Model Cheats</a>\n   675→                            </div>\n   676→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   677→                                Research on prompt-level mitigation of model cheating behaviors. 75 points, 56 comments discussing the findings.\n   678→                            </div>\n   679→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   680→                                <span class=\"item-source\">Hacker News</span>\n   681→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-16</span>\n   682→                            </div>\n   683→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   684→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">LLM</span>\n   685→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">safety</span>\n   686→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">adversarial</span>\n   687→                            </div>\n   688→                        </div>\n   689→\n   690→                        <!-- ComponentBench -->\n   691→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   692→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   693→                                <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\" target=\"_blank\">ComponentBench: Diagnosing Component-Level Failures in Computer-Use Agents</a>\n   694→                            </div>\n   695→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   696→                                Accepted at COLM 2026. Benchmark for testing agent components at the component level.\n   697→                            </div>\n   698→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   699→                                <span class=\"item-source\">ArXiv</span>\n   700→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-20</span>\n   701→                            </div>\n   702→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   703→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">agents</span>\n   704→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">benchmarks</span>\n   705→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">COLM 2026</span>\n   706→                            </div>\n   707→                        </div>\n   708→\n   709→                        <!-- A Jagged Frontier -->\n   710→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   711→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   712→                                <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\" target=\"_blank\">A Jagged Frontier: Evaluating Robustness of Code Agents to Semantics-Preserving Transformations</a>\n   713→                            </div>\n   714→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   715→                                Evaluates code agents against transformations that preserve semantics. Authors from Colorado State University, Microsoft, UIUC, and Carnegie Mellon.\n   716→                            </div>\n   717→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   718→                                <span class=\"item-source\">ArXiv</span>\n   719→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-20</span>\n   720→                            </div>\n   721→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   722→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">code agents</span>\n   723→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">robustness</span>\n   724→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">evaluation</span>\n   725→                            </div>\n   726→                        </div>\n   727→\n   728→                        <!-- Adversarial Review -->\n   729→                        <div class=\"item\">\n   730→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   731→                                <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/recent\" target=\"_blank\">Adversarial Review: Structured Disagreement for Grounded Agentic Code Review</a>\n   732→                            </div>\n   733→                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n   734→                                Accepted to ICML 2026 Workshop on DL4C. Focuses on automated code review methodologies using structured disagreement.\n   735→                            </div>\n   736→                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   737→                                <span class=\"item-source\">ArXiv</span>\n   738→                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-20</span>\n   739→                            </div>\n   740→                            <div class=\"topics\">\n   741→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">code review</span>\n   742→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">agents</span>\n   743→                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">ICML 2026</span>\n   744→                            </div>\n   745→                        </div>\n   746→                    </div>\n   747→                </section>\n   748→            </div>\n   749→        </main>\n   750→\n   751→        <footer>\n   752→            <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n   753→            <a href=\"#\">Archive</a>\n   754→            <a href=\"#\">RSS Feed</a>\n   755→            <a href=\"#\">Contact</a>\n   756→            <div style=\"margin-top: 10px; color: #828282; font-size: 11px;\">\n   757→                Generated with Claude Code | Agentic Coding Research Report\n   758→            </div>\n   759→        </footer>\n   760→    </div>\n   761→</body>\n   762→</html>"
