          "                 <section class=\"column technical-insights\" id=\"technical-insights\">",
          "                     <div class=\"section-header\">Technical Insights</div>",
          "                     <div class=\"section-content\">",
          "-                        <!-- Huzzah AI Coding Approach -->",
          "+                        <!-- Stop Making TUIs -->",
          "                         <div class=\"item\">",
          "                             <div class=\"item-title\">",
          "-                                <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Show HN: Huzzah – Novel AI Coding Approach</a>",
          "+                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Stop Making TUIs - Native UIs for AI Coding Era</a>",
          "                             </div>",
          "                             <div class=\"item-description\">",
          "-                                New method for programming with AI assistance. Community discussion with 196 points and 110 comments.",
          "+                                Thomas Ptacek advocates for building real native user interfaces for even the smallest of personal tools, because coding agents have reduced the cost of getting a usable-enough GUI up and running to almost nothing. Simon notes he's still using his vibe-coded bandwidth and GPU monitoring macOS task bar apps built in March.",
          "                             </div>",
          "                             <div class=\"item-meta\">",
          "-                                <span class=\"item-source\">Hacker News</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison (Blog)</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-21</span>",
          "+                            </div>",
          "+                            <div class=\"topics\">",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">vibe-coding</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">coding-agents</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">native UIs</span>",
          "+                            </div>",
          "+                        </div>",
          "+",
          "+                        <!-- ChatGPT Search Site Operator -->",
          "+                        <div class=\"item\">",
          "+                            <div class=\"item-title\">",
          "+                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">ChatGPT search now uses the site: operator at scale</a>",
          "+                            </div>",
          "+                            <div class=\"item-description\">",
          "+                                Promptwatch tracking shows ChatGPT Search usage of site: operator jumped from 0.3-0.5% to 16-17% around August 8, correlating with GPT-5.6 Sol rollout. On August 18th, Promptwatch reported ChatGPT appeared to have greatly reduced the likelihood of Reddit being used in those searches.",
          "+                            </div>",
          "+                            <div class=\"item-meta\">",
          "+                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison (Blog)</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-20</span>",
          "+                            </div>",
          "+                            <div class=\"topics\">",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">chatgpt</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">search</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">site:operator</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">openai</span>",
          "+                            </div>",
          "+                        </div>",
          "+",
          "+                        <!-- Bun 1.4 WebView -->",
          "+                        <div class=\"item\">",
          "+                            <div class=\"item-title\">",
          "+                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Bun 1.4 adds Bun.WebView for browser automation</a>",
          "+                            </div>",
          "+                            <div class=\"item-description\">",
          "+                                Bun 1.4 release adds Bun.WebView for first-class browser automation support using either macOS WebKit or control of a local Chromium process via CDP. Simon prototyped a web API with Claude Code for web that loads pages and executes JavaScript, inspired by shot-scraper.",
          "+                            </div>",
          "+                            <div class=\"item-meta\">",
          "+                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison (Blog)</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-20</span>",
          "+                            </div>",
          "+                            <div class=\"topics\">",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">bun</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">javascript</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">browsers</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">coding-agents</span>",
          "+                            </div>",
          "+                        </div>",
          "+",
          "+                        <!-- smolmachines sandbox -->",
          "+                        <div class=\"item\">",
          "+                            <div class=\"item-title\">",
          "+                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">smolmachines / smolvm as a sandbox for untrusted Python & JavaScript</a>",
          "+                            </div>",
          "+                            <div class=\"item-description\">",
          "+                                Research task testing smolmachines.com as a fast secure sandbox for running untrusted Python and JavaScript code with limits on RAM, CPU time, no network access, and controlled filesystem access. Claude Fable 5 creatively worked around Claude Code for web environment limits by running tests via GitHub Actions.",
          "+                            </div>",
          "+                            <div class=\"item-meta\">",
          "+                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison (Blog)</span>",
          "                                 <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-19</span>",
          "                             </div>",
          "                             <div class=\"topics\">",
          "-                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">AI coding</span>",
          "-                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">Show HN</span>",
          "-                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">programming tools</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">research</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">sandboxing</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">claude-mythos-fable</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">github-actions</span>",
          "                             </div>",
          "                         </div>",
          " ",
          "-                        <!-- Stop Anthropomorphizing Tokens -->",
          "+                        <!-- Mojo Open Source -->",
          "                         <div class=\"item\">",
          "                             <div class=\"item-title\">",
          "-                                <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Stop Anthropomorphizing Intermediate Tokens</a>",
          "+                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Mojo🔥 is now open source</a>",
          "                             </div>",
          "                             <div class=\"item-description\">",
          "-                                Paper argues against interpreting middle tokens as reasoning. 189 points, 105 comments on Hacker News.",
          "+                                Mojo programming language released compiler and toolchain under Apache 2 license. Originally planned as Python superset, that plan changed around August 2025. Today Mojo is its own language optimized for GPU programming with Python-inspired syntax.",
          "                             </div>",
          "                             <div class=\"item-meta\">",
          "-                                <span class=\"item-source\">Hacker News</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison (Blog)</span>",
          "                                 <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-18</span>",
          "                             </div>",
          "                             <div class=\"topics\">",
          "-                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">LLM</span>",
          "-                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">tokens</span>",
          "-                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">reasoning</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">mojo</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">open-source</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">python</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">gpu-programming</span>",
          "                             </div>",
          "                         </div>",
          " ",
          "-                        <!-- Vomit Claude Token Output -->",
          "+                        <!-- Qwen 3.8 Performance -->",
          "                         <div class=\"item\">",
          "                             <div class=\"item-title\">",
          "-                                <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Vomit: Cleaning Claude 5 Token Output</a>",
          "+                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Qwen 3.8 27B scores 52 on Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index</a>",
          "                             </div>",
          "                             <div class=\"item-description\">",
          "-                                Uses separate LLM to refine another model's output. 169 points, 184 comments discussing the technique.",
          "+                                Qwen 3.8 27B matches GPT-5.6 Luna performance (score 52), just one point behind GLM-5.2 (753B) and DeepSeek V4 Pro 0813 (1.7T). Qwen is a truly astonishing 27B parameter Apache 2 licensed model.",
          "                             </div>",
          "                             <div class=\"item-meta\">",
          "-                                <span class=\"item-source\">Hacker News</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison (Blog)</span>",
          "                                 <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-17</span>",
          "                             </div>",
          "                             <div class=\"topics\">",
          "-                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">Claude</span>",
          "-                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">LLM</span>",
          "-                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">output refinement</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">qwen</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">llm</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">local-llms</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">open-source</span>",
          "                             </div>",
          "                         </div>",
          " ",
          "-                        <!-- Qwen 3.8 Performance -->",
          "+                        <!-- Amazon AI Training Books -->",
          "                         <div class=\"item\">",
          "                             <div class=\"item-title\">",
          "-                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Qwen 3.8 27B matches GPT-5.6 Luna performance</a>",
          "+                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">We Tracked a Shipment of Rare Books. It Ended at an Amazon AI Training Facility</a>",
          "                             </div>",
          "                             <div class=\"item-description\">",
          "-                                Qwen 3.8 27B stands out as an impressive Apache 2-licensed 27B model that scores 52 on Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index—matching GPT-5.6 Luna.",
          "+                                404 Media investigated with an AirTag where large-volume book orders from anonymous suspected AI training customers actually go. The book ended at Amazon's LAS8 facility in Las Vegas, confirmed by worker discussions to destructively scan large volumes of books for AI training.",
          "                             </div>",
          "                             <div class=\"item-meta\">",
          "-                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"item-source\">Simon Willison (Blog)</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"item-date\">2026-08-17</span>",
          "+                            </div>",
          "+                            <div class=\"topics\">",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">amazon</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">journalism</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">ai-ethics</span>",
          "+                                <span class=\"topic-tag\">404-media</span>",
          "+                            </div>",
          "+                        </div>",
          "+",
          "+                        <!-- Qwen Overthinking -->",
          "+                        <div class=\"item\">",
          "+                            <div class=\"item-title\">",
          "+                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Qwen 3.8 27B is excellent, but it defaults to wildly overthinking things</a>",
